{
  "info": {
    "name": "HR Vision System — Backend Service API",
    "description": "Laravel backend for the employee activity tracking system.\n\n## Getting started\n1. Set the `base_url` variable (default `http://localhost:8000/api`).\n2. Set `user_name` and `password`.\n3. Run **Auth → POST /login**. Its test script writes the returned token into the `token` collection variable, and every other request inherits Bearer auth from the collection — no manual copying.\n\n## Auth & roles\nLaravel Sanctum bearer tokens. Logging in **deletes the user's existing tokens**, so a second login invalidates the first session.\n\nEvery route except `/login` also passes through `check.idel` (idle-timeout) and an `authorization` middleware. Each folder/request notes which roles are allowed:\n- HR Manager, CEO, HR Employee — day-to-day operations\n- HR Manager, CEO — create/destroy users, employees, zones\n- CEO only — roles, password resets, audit logs\n\nA 403 usually means the role gate, not a bad token.\n\n## Conventions worth knowing\n- **Updates that accept a file use POST, not PUT** (`/employees/update/{id}`, `/camera/update/{id}`) because they're `multipart/form-data`. PUT is used only for JSON-only updates.\n- Field names follow the database as-is, including `Administration` (capital A), `direct_maneger`, and `sheft`.\n- Employees are soft-deleted; uniqueness rules on `job_num` and `card_id` only consider non-deleted rows.\n- File-upload requests have their body rows pre-created but empty — pick a local file in Postman before sending.\n- Video uploads: mp4/mov/avi/mkv, max 512000 KB. Images: jpg/jpeg/png/webp, max 2048 KB.\n\n## Vision pipeline ordering\nCheck-in seeds the day's body-fingerprint gallery, so it must run before zone cameras for that date. `POST /process-sequence` does the whole daily flow in the correct order — reach for it instead of chaining `/checkin` and `/cameras/process-batch` by hand.\n\nGenerated from `routes/api.php` and the controller validation rules.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000/api",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Backend root + /api"
    },
    {
      "key": "user_name",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Populated automatically by the login request's test script."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "description": "Sanctum token auth. `POST /login` deletes any prior tokens for the user, so only one session per account is valid at a time.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/login"
            },
            "description": "Public. Returns `{token, user}`. Rate limited by `throttle:login`.\n\nRules:\n- `user_name` required|string\n- `password` required|string\n\n401 on bad credentials.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"user_name\": \"{{user_name}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "if (res.token) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', res.token);",
                  "  console.log('token saved to collection variable {{token}}');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /logout",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/logout"
            },
            "description": "Deletes all of the current user's tokens. Roles: HR Manager, CEO, HR Employee."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
