    {
      "name": "Vision Processing",
      "description": "Dispatches video to the vision service and tracks the resulting jobs.\n\nOrdering matters: check-in must run **before** zone cameras for a given day, because it seeds that day's body-fingerprint gallery. `POST /process-sequence` does both in the right order in one call — prefer it over calling check-in and batch separately.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /camera/1/process",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/camera/1/process"
            },
            "description": "Process one camera's video. Roles: HR Manager, CEO, HR Employee.\n\nRules:\n- `session_date` nullable|date (defaults to the camera's own session)\n- `write_video` nullable|boolean — write an annotated output video\n- `annotate_stride` nullable|integer|min:1 — annotate every Nth frame; higher = faster, coarser",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"session_date\": \"2026-08-21\",\n  \"write_video\": true,\n  \"annotate_stride\": 5\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /cameras/process-batch",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/cameras/process-batch"
            },
            "description": "Process several cameras against one session date. Roles: HR Manager, CEO, HR Employee.\n\nRules:\n- `camera_ids` required|array|min:1, each `exists:cameras,id`\n- `session_date`, `write_video`, `annotate_stride` as above",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"camera_ids\": [\n    1,\n    2,\n    3\n  ],\n  \"session_date\": \"2026-08-21\",\n  \"write_video\": false,\n  \"annotate_stride\": 5\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /process-sequence",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/process-sequence"
            },
            "description": "**The full daily flow in one call.** Runs check-in first (seeding that day's body-fingerprint gallery in the vision service), then processes the given zone cameras against that same day.\n\nSent as `multipart/form-data` here so `checkin_video` can be a file upload. If you're using `checkin_camera_id` instead of a file, a plain JSON body works too:\n\n```json\n{\"checkin_camera_id\": 1, \"camera_ids\": [2,3], \"write_video\": false, \"annotate_stride\": 5}\n```",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "checkin_video",
                  "type": "file",
                  "description": "nullable|file — mp4, mov, avi, mkv — max 512000 KB. Use this OR `checkin_camera_id`, not both.",
                  "src": []
                },
                {
                  "key": "checkin_camera_id",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "nullable — a single integer, or repeat `checkin_camera_id[]` for several. Each must exist in cameras.",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "camera_ids[]",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "required|array|min:1 — repeat this key per camera id.",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "camera_ids[]",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "required|array|min:1 — repeat this key per camera id.",
                  "value": "2"
                },
                {
                  "key": "write_video",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "nullable|boolean",
                  "value": "0"
                },
                {
                  "key": "annotate_stride",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "nullable|integer|min:1",
                  "value": "5"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
